    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0811" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3059: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-13T20:00:00+01:00">December 13,
                            1935—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 13—5:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>653. The Secretariat circulated this afternoon: the text of the Fronco-British
                    proposals for a settlement of the Italo-Abyssinian dispute;<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d580-f1"/> a communications from the Abyssinian Government to the
                        <pb facs="0812" n="710" xml:id="pg710"/> Secretary General dated today in
                    regard to the proposals;<anchor n="19" xml:id="d580-f2"/> the reply of the
                    Secretary General to the latter.</p>
                <p>I am informed that full texts are being telegraphed by the American press
                    agencies here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
